    "dependency-hygiene": {
      "name": "dependency-hygiene",
      "description": "Clean up pyproject.toml and library dependencies: remove unused jwcrypto/django-markup/cbor2, move test-only packages to dev group, complete bleach to nh3 migration, complete pytz to zoneinfo migration, replace pandas with openpyxl for single read_excel call, remove backport importlib_metadata",
      "issue_ids": [
        "review::.::holistic::dependency_health::declared_but_unused_deps",
        "review::.::holistic::dependency_health::dual_importlib_metadata",
        "review::.::holistic::dependency_health::test_deps_in_production",
        "review::.::holistic::dependency_health::incomplete_bleach_to_nh3_migration",
        "review::.::holistic::dependency_health::pandas_for_single_excel_read",
        "review::.::holistic::dependency_health::dual_timezone_pytz_zoneinfo",
        "review::.::holistic::incomplete_migration::pytz_zoneinfo_mixed_migration",
        "review::.::holistic::dependency_health::dual_html_sanitizer",
        "review::.::holistic::dependency_health::dual_pdf_libs",
        "review::.::holistic::dependency_health::heavy_analytics_deps",
        "review::.::holistic::dependency_health::python_version_blocker",
        "review::.::holistic::dependency_health::unpinned_git_deps"
      ],
      "created_at": "2026-03-14T14:58:24+00:00",
      "updated_at": "2026-03-16T07:25:55+00:00",
      "auto": false,
      "cluster_key": "",
      "action": null,
      "user_modified": true,
      "action_steps": [
        {
          "title": "Remove unused and misplaced dependencies from pyproject.toml",
          "detail": "In app/pyproject.toml: remove 'jwcrypto>=1.5.6' (line 119), 'cbor2>=5.8.0' (line 38), 'django-markup>=1.9.1' (line 83) from production dependencies \u2014 none have import sites in app/eventyay/ (verify with grep -rn 'import jwcrypto\\|import cbor2\\|import django_markup' app/eventyay/). Move 'responses>=0.25.5' (line 178), 'pycodestyle>=2.12.1' (line 149), 'execnet>=2.1.2' (line 104) to the [tool.uv.dev-dependencies] or equivalent test group in pyproject.toml. In app/eventyay/config/settings.py lines 5 and 11: stdlib importlib.metadata is imported at line 5 ('from importlib.metadata import entry_points') and the backport importlib_metadata is imported at line 11 and used at line 369 ('eps = importlib_metadata.entry_points()'). Delete the importlib_metadata import at line 11, replace line 369 with 'eps = entry_points()' using the stdlib version already imported at line 5. Remove 'importlib-metadata>=8.7.1' (line 113) from pyproject.toml.",
          "effort": "small",
          "issue_refs": [
            "review::.::holistic::dependency_health::declared_but_unused_deps",
            "review::.::holistic::dependency_health::dual_importlib_metadata",
            "review::.::holistic::dependency_health::test_deps_in_production"
          ]
        },
        {
          "title": "Complete bleach to nh3 migration and replace pandas with openpyxl",
          "detail": "In app/eventyay/base/templatetags/rich_text.py: this file has 6 bleach imports (lines 7, 10, 12) and 4 TODO markers requesting nh3 migration. Replace bleach.Cleaner with nh3.clean() calls directly: nh3 does not support linkification, so extract the link-rewriting logic (link_callback at line 87) into a post-sanitize pass using Python html.parser. Replace CLEANER.clean() calls with nh3.clean(text, tags=ALLOWED_TAGS, attributes=ALLOWED_ATTRIBUTES) + apply_links(). In app/eventyay/storage/schedule_to_json.py line 31: 'pandas.read_excel(...)' is the only pandas call in the codebase. Replace with openpyxl: 'from openpyxl import load_workbook; wb = load_workbook(filename=path); ws = wb.active; data = [row for row in ws.values]'. Remove 'bleach>=6.3.0' and 'pandas>=2.3.3' from app/pyproject.toml after migration. Add 'openpyxl' to pyproject.toml if not already present.",
          "effort": "medium",
          "issue_refs": [
            "review::.::holistic::dependency_health::incomplete_bleach_to_nh3_migration",
            "review::.::holistic::dependency_health::pandas_for_single_excel_read",
            "review::.::holistic::dependency_health::dual_html_sanitizer"
          ]
        },
        {
          "title": "Migrate all 29 pytz usages to zoneinfo",
          "detail": "Run: grep -rn 'import pytz' app/eventyay/ --include='*.py' to get the 29 files. Confirmed files include: app/eventyay/core/management/commands/export.py, app/eventyay/core/management/commands/clear_unused_events.py, app/eventyay/plugins/reports/exporters.py, app/eventyay/features/importers/conftool.py, app/eventyay/features/analytics/graphs/tasks.py, app/eventyay/features/analytics/graphs/report.py, app/eventyay/features/analytics/graphs/views.py, app/eventyay/presale/ical.py, app/eventyay/presale/views/event.py, app/eventyay/presale/views/widget.py, and ~19 more. In each file: replace 'import pytz' with 'from zoneinfo import ZoneInfo'; replace 'pytz.timezone(tz_name)' with 'ZoneInfo(tz_name)'; replace 'pytz.utc' with 'datetime.timezone.utc'; replace 'dt.astimezone(pytz.timezone(...))' with 'dt.astimezone(ZoneInfo(...))'. After all files are updated, remove 'pytz>=2025.2' from app/pyproject.toml.",
          "effort": "large",
          "issue_refs": [
            "review::.::holistic::dependency_health::dual_timezone_pytz_zoneinfo",
            "review::.::holistic::dependency_health::dual_pdf_libs",
            "review::.::holistic::dependency_health::heavy_analytics_deps",
            "review::.::holistic::dependency_health::python_version_blocker",
            "review::.::holistic::dependency_health::unpinned_git_deps"
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
