    "api-views-auth-bypass": {
      "name": "api-views-auth-bypass",
      "description": "Fix authentication bypass pattern in api/views/event.py: hook CreateEventView and EventThemeView into standard DRF auth/permission classes instead of rolling empty authentication_classes and manual JWT parsing inline",
      "issue_ids": [
        "review::.::holistic::authorization_consistency::ac-01",
        "review::.::holistic::authorization_consistency::ac-02",
        "review::.::holistic::authorization_consistency::ac-03",
        "review::.::holistic::authorization_consistency::ac-04",
        "review::.::holistic::authorization_consistency::admin_mode_bypass_no_audit"
      ],
      "created_at": "2026-03-15T09:33:02+00:00",
      "updated_at": "2026-03-16T07:10:35+00:00",
      "auto": false,
      "cluster_key": "",
      "action": null,
      "user_modified": true,
      "action_steps": [
        {
          "title": "Wire CreateEventView and UserFavouriteView into DRF JWTAuthentication class and remove inline _extract_bearer_token",
          "detail": "In app/eventyay/api/views/event.py lines 483-500 and 604-660: CreateEventView has authentication_classes = [] (line 484) and calls _extract_bearer_token() inline (line 594); UserFavouriteView (line 604) has permission_classes = [] and calls _extract_bearer_token() (line 657). Replace authentication_classes = [] with authentication_classes = [JWTAuthentication] from rest_framework_simplejwt.authentication. Remove calls to _extract_bearer_token and extract user from request.user instead. Delete the _extract_bearer_token helper (lines 58-75) once no callers remain.",
          "effort": "medium",
          "issue_refs": [
            "review::.::holistic::authorization_consistency::ac-01",
            "review::.::holistic::authorization_consistency::ac-02"
          ]
        },
        {
          "title": "Add permission comment to EventThemeView and audit admin bypass in ActionFromUrl._check_permission",
          "detail": "In app/eventyay/api/views/event.py line 459: EventThemeView has permission_classes = [] with no comment. Add an inline comment explaining why public access is intentional. In app/eventyay/common/views/mixins.py, find ActionFromUrl._check_permission and add audit log call (LogEntry.objects.create or equivalent) on the admin bypass path so security decisions are traceable.",
          "effort": "small",
          "issue_refs": [
            "review::.::holistic::authorization_consistency::ac-03",
            "review::.::holistic::authorization_consistency::ac-04"
          ]
        },
        {
          "title": "Write tests for the corrected DRF auth integration in api/views/event.py",
          "detail": "In app/tests/stable/test_api.py or a new app/tests/stable/test_auth_views.py: add test cases for CreateEventView and UserFavouriteView that send requests with no token, an expired token, and a valid token. Verify the invalid-token cases return HTTP 401 (not 500). Use DRF APIClient and SimpleJWT token factory to generate test tokens.",
          "effort": "small",
          "issue_refs": [
            "review::.::holistic::authorization_consistency::ac-01",
            "review::.::holistic::authorization_consistency::ac-02"
          ]
        },
        {
          "title": "Verify no other views in api/ have authentication_classes = [] without documented rationale",
          "detail": "Run: grep -rn 'authentication_classes = \\[\\]\\|permission_classes = \\[\\]' app/eventyay/api/views/ to get full list. For each hit, either add DRF auth class or add a docstring comment with rationale like '# public endpoint: no auth required because X'. File: app/eventyay/api/views/event.py is the primary file; check all files in app/eventyay/api/views/ directory.",
          "effort": "small",
          "issue_refs": [
            "review::.::holistic::authorization_consistency::ac-03",
            "review::.::holistic::authorization_consistency::ac-04"
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    "service-function-signatures": {
      "name": "service-function-signatures",
      "description": "Normalize inconsistent function signatures across base/services/orders.py and base/services/checkin.py: standardize user/auth parameter order, replace int PKs with model instances, reduce perform_checkin arity, document error contracts",
      "issue_ids": [
        "review::.::holistic::api_surface_coherence::asc-01",
        "review::.::holistic::api_surface_coherence::asc-07",
        "review::.::holistic::api_surface_coherence::asc-02",
        "review::.::holistic::api_surface_coherence::asc-03",
        "review::.::holistic::api_surface_coherence::asc-04",
        "review::.::holistic::api_surface_coherence::asc-05",
        "review::.::holistic::api_surface_coherence::asc-06",
        "review::.::holistic::api_surface_coherence::AC-01",
        "review::.::holistic::api_surface_coherence::AC-02",
        "review::.::holistic::contract_coherence::CC-04"
      ],
      "created_at": "2026-03-15T09:33:31+00:00",
      "updated_at": "2026-03-16T11:16:57+00:00",
      "auto": false,
      "cluster_key": "",
      "action": null,
      "user_modified": true,
      "action_steps": [
        {
          "title": "Normalize user/auth parameter order in approve_order, deny_order, reactivate_order and _cancel_order",
          "detail": "In app/eventyay/base/services/orders.py: standardize user/auth parameter ordering across 4 functions. Current state: reactivate_order (line 153) is (order, force, user, auth); approve_order (line 286) is (order, user, send_mail, auth, force); deny_order (line 359) is (order, comment, user, send_mail, auth); _cancel_order (line 426) is (order, user, send_mail, api_token, device, oauth_application, cancellation_fee, keep_fees, cancel_invoice) \u2014 9 positional params. Standardize all to signature (order, *, user=None, auth=None, force=False, send_mail=True, ...) using bare * to make all params after order keyword-only. This requires updating all call sites \u2014 grep -rn 'approve_order\\|deny_order\\|reactivate_order\\|_cancel_order' app/eventyay/ to find them (primary callers are in control/views/orders.py and api/views/order.py).",
          "effort": "medium",
          "issue_refs": [
            "review::.::holistic::api_surface_coherence::asc-01",
            "review::.::holistic::api_surface_coherence::asc-07"
          ]
        },
        {
          "title": "Fix cancel_order Celery task to accept model instances or explicit int-pk overload",
          "detail": "In app/eventyay/base/services/orders.py line 2668: cancel_order Celery task signature has 'order: int' and 'user: int = None'. The task at line 2684 passes order and user directly to _cancel_order which also accepts int (due to isinstance(order, int) check at line 444). Change 'user: int = None' to 'user: int | None = None' (fixes invalid annotation). For order: document that the int is an order PK \u2014 add a comment '# PK of Order, not a model instance (Celery serialization constraint)'. Grep for all callers of cancel_order.delay() and cancel_order.apply_async() to verify they all pass PKs: grep -rn 'cancel_order.delay\\|cancel_order.apply_async' app/eventyay/. Also update 'user: int = None' pattern in mail_send_task (app/eventyay/base/services/mail.py line 344) consistently.",
          "effort": "small",
          "issue_refs": [
            "review::.::holistic::api_surface_coherence::asc-02"
          ]
        },
        {
          "title": "Reduce perform_checkin arity and fix BaseExporter.render return type annotation",
          "detail": "In app/eventyay/base/services/checkin.py line 377: perform_checkin has 12 params (op, clist, given_answers, force, ignore_unpaid, nonce, datetime, questions_supported, user, auth, canceled_supported, type). Create a dataclass CheckinContext at top of the file: '@dataclass class CheckinContext: user: Any = None; auth: Any = None; force: bool = False; ignore_unpaid: bool = False; nonce: str | None = None; datetime: Any = None; questions_supported: bool = True; canceled_supported: bool = False; type: str = Checkin.TYPE_ENTRY'. Update perform_checkin signature to (op, clist, given_answers, context: CheckinContext | None = None) and update body to unpack context attributes. Update all callers: grep -rn 'perform_checkin(' app/eventyay/ to find call sites. In app/eventyay/base/exporter.py line 94: BaseExporter.render() return type is '-> Tuple[str, str, bytes]' but ListExporter.render (line 221) and TablularExporter.render (line 350) accept output_file parameter and return None when output_file is provided. Change base annotation to '-> Tuple[str, str, bytes] | None'. In app/eventyay/base/services/orders.py line 2712: replace 'raise Exception(change_payment_provider should only be called in atomic transaction\\!)' with a 'class NotInTransactionError(RuntimeError): pass' defined at top of file and raise that.",
          "effort": "large",
          "issue_refs": [
            "review::.::holistic::api_surface_coherence::asc-03",
            "review::.::holistic::api_surface_coherence::asc-04",
            "review::.::holistic::api_surface_coherence::asc-05",
            "review::.::holistic::api_surface_coherence::asc-06",
            "review::.::holistic::api_surface_coherence::AC-01",
            "review::.::holistic::api_surface_coherence::AC-02",
            "review::.::holistic::contract_coherence::CC-04"
          ]
        }
      ],
      "depends_on_clusters": [
        "design-coherence-fixes"
      ]
    },
    "service-return-contracts": {
      "name": "service-return-contracts",
      "description": "Fix undocumented and inconsistent return value contracts in base/services/orders.py and base/services/checkin.py: approve_order/deny_order return pk silently, mark_order_refunded hides dual-role auth param, perform_checkin returns bare None on nonce match, build_time has implicit None fallback",
      "issue_ids": [
        "subjective::contract_coherence",
        "review::.::holistic::contract_coherence::cc-04",
        "review::.::holistic::contract_coherence::cc-06",
        "review::.::holistic::contract_coherence::cc-03",
        "review::.::holistic::contract_coherence::cc-05",
        "review::.::holistic::contract_coherence::cc-07",
        "review::.::holistic::api_surface_coherence::AC-03",
        "review::.::holistic::contract_coherence::CC-01",
        "review::.::holistic::contract_coherence::CC-02",
        "review::.::holistic::contract_coherence::CC-03",
        "review::.::holistic::logic_clarity::LC-01"
      ],
      "created_at": "2026-03-15T09:34:09+00:00",
      "updated_at": "2026-03-16T07:14:42+00:00",
      "auto": false,
      "cluster_key": "",
      "action": null,
      "user_modified": true,
      "action_steps": [
        {
          "title": "Document approve_order/deny_order return value and mark_order_refunded auth dispatch",
          "detail": "In app/eventyay/base/services/orders.py: approve_order (line 290) returns order.pk implicitly with no annotation; add -> int return annotation. deny_order (line 363) similarly returns order.pk; add -> int annotation. For mark_order_refunded (line 252): its auth param is used via isinstance(auth, TeamAPIToken)/isinstance(auth, Device) dispatch at lines 266-275 \u2014 refactor to Union[TeamAPIToken, Device, OAuthApplication, None] in the signature and document the dispatch logic.",
          "effort": "small",
          "issue_refs": [
            "review::.::holistic::contract_coherence::cc-04",
            "review::.::holistic::contract_coherence::cc-06"
          ]
        },
        {
          "title": "Fix perform_checkin nonce-match silent return and build_time implicit None fallback",
          "detail": "In app/eventyay/base/services/checkin.py at line 472: perform_checkin has a bare 'return' (no value) when nonce matches; add explicit 'return None' and add -> Optional[CheckInError] to the function return type (currently unannotated), updating docstring to note the nonce-match case. At lines 53-61: build_time inner function in get_logic_environment returns None implicitly for unhandled time types; add raise ValueError(f'Unhandled time type: {type(t)}') to make the failure explicit.",
          "effort": "small",
          "issue_refs": [
            "review::.::holistic::contract_coherence::cc-03",
            "review::.::holistic::contract_coherence::cc-05"
          ]
        },
        {
          "title": "Fix CompatibleCountryField.to_representation return type annotation",
          "detail": "In app/eventyay/api/serializers/order.py at line 65: CompatibleCountryField.to_representation (class defined at line 61) returns either instance.country.code (str) or str(instance.country) (str) or None with no return annotation. Add '-> Optional[str]' annotation and document that None is returned when country field is empty. Also add '-> Optional[str]' to the CountryField.to_representation at line 76.",
          "effort": "trivial",
          "issue_refs": [
            "review::.::holistic::contract_coherence::cc-07"
          ]
        }
      ],
      "depends_on_clusters": [
        "design-coherence-fixes"
      ]
    },
    "presale-order-view-fixes": {
      "name": "presale-order-view-fixes",
      "description": "Fix OrderDetailMixin.order property in presale/views/order.py: dead else-else both returning None with misleading timing-attack comment, and fix presale/utils.py _detect_event 160-line function mixing three domain-resolution paths",
      "issue_ids": [
        "review::.::holistic::contract_coherence::cc-01",
        "review::.::holistic::logic_clarity::lc-01",
        "review::.::holistic::low_level_elegance::lle-01",
        "review::.::holistic::low_level_elegance::lle-05",
        "review::.::holistic::logic_clarity::lc-03",
        "review::.::holistic::logic_clarity::lc-04",
        "review::.::holistic::low_level_elegance::detect_event_monolith",
        "review::.::holistic::mid_level_elegance::locale_middleware_sentinel"
      ],
      "created_at": "2026-03-15T09:34:43+00:00",
      "updated_at": "2026-03-16T07:12:30+00:00",
      "auto": false,
      "cluster_key": "",
      "action": null,
      "user_modified": true,
      "action_steps": [
        {
          "title": "Fix OrderDetailMixin.order dead-else-else logic and clarify timing-attack comment",
          "detail": "In app/eventyay/presale/views/order.py lines 102-114: OrderDetailMixin.order property has 'if order:' / 'if order.secret.lower() == ...: return order / else: return None' / 'else: # Do a comparison to harden timing attacks / if ... == ...: return None / else: return None'. Both branches of the outer else return None making the timing-attack comparison dead. Remove lines 110-114 (outer else block), keep only lines 103-108 (order exists case). The timing comparison was supposed to be the alternative return path but it compares a hardcoded string, so the comment is misleading.",
          "effort": "trivial",
          "issue_refs": [
            "review::.::holistic::contract_coherence::cc-01",
            "review::.::holistic::logic_clarity::lc-01"
          ]
        },
        {
          "title": "Decompose _detect_event and extract session key constant",
          "detail": "In app/eventyay/presale/utils.py at line 29: _detect_event is a 160-line function mixing domain resolution via (1) hostname, (2) organizer slug, (3) event slug paths. Split into three helpers: _resolve_event_by_domain(request), _resolve_event_by_organizer_slug(request, organizer, event), _resolve_event_by_access_key(request). Extract the session key 'eventyay_event_access_{}'.format(request.event.pk) (duplicated at lines 106-107) into a module-level constant EVENT_ACCESS_SESSION_KEY = 'eventyay_event_access_{}'.",
          "effort": "medium",
          "issue_refs": [
            "review::.::holistic::low_level_elegance::lle-01",
            "review::.::holistic::low_level_elegance::lle-05"
          ]
        },
        {
          "title": "Fix cfp_session premature session.modified and pre-transaction race in perform_checkin",
          "detail": "In app/eventyay/cfp/flow.py at line 80: cfp_session() sets request.session.modified = True immediately on function entry (line 80) before any write to session data, causing the session to be saved on every read-only call. Move 'request.session.modified = True' to after the first actual session write in the function. In app/eventyay/base/services/checkin.py at line 407: the pre-transaction status check op.order.status races with the transaction-safe lock; add a comment documenting that this check is an optimistic early-exit and the authoritative check happens inside the transaction lock.",
          "effort": "small",
          "issue_refs": [
            "review::.::holistic::logic_clarity::lc-03",
            "review::.::holistic::logic_clarity::lc-04"
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    "abstraction-layer-cleanup": {
      "name": "abstraction-layer-cleanup",
      "description": "Remove or justify thin abstraction wrappers: parse_ics_token one-line pass-through in agenda/views/utils.py, deprecated event_view wrapper in presale/utils.py, FakeStatsD/StatsD protocol class in core/utils/statsd.py, and announcement service **kwargs pass-through in base/services/announcement.py",
