    "error-handling-standardization": {
      "name": "error-handling-standardization",
      "description": "Replace bare Exception raises and silent swallows in production code: 30+ bare Exception() calls in domain services, FileCleanupMixin.save swallowing all exceptions, replay attack detection using bare Exception, user-facing validation raising bare Exception, GeoCodeView collapsing error types",
      "issue_ids": [
        "review::.::holistic::error_consistency::err_security_bare_exception",
        "review::.::holistic::error_consistency::err_user_validation_bare_exception",
        "review::.::holistic::error_consistency::err_file_cleanup_silent_swallow",
        "review::.::holistic::error_consistency::err_geo_silent_mixed_failure",
        "review::.::holistic::error_consistency::err_bare_exception_domain_violations",
        "review::.::holistic::error_consistency::err-001",
        "review::.::holistic::error_consistency::err-002",
        "review::.::holistic::error_consistency::err-004",
        "review::.::holistic::error_consistency::err-005"
      ],
      "created_at": "2026-03-15T09:37:52+00:00",
      "updated_at": "2026-03-16T11:14:31+00:00",
      "auto": false,
      "cluster_key": "",
      "action": null,
      "user_modified": true,
      "action_steps": [
        {
          "title": "Replace bare Exception() raises in security and validation code with domain exceptions",
          "detail": "In app/eventyay/eventyay_common/views/auth.py lines 485 and 498: 'raise Exception(Possible replay attack...)'. A RepeatedResetDenied class already exists at line 310 in the same file but is unrelated. Create class ReplayAttackDetected(Exception) at the top of app/eventyay/eventyay_common/views/auth.py (or in a new app/eventyay/eventyay_common/exceptions.py). Replace both bare Exception raises with 'raise ReplayAttackDetected(...)'. In app/eventyay/control/views/user.py lines 81 and 94: same replay attack pattern \u2014 replace with 'raise ReplayAttackDetected(...)' importing from eventyay_common.exceptions. In app/eventyay/orga/forms/cfp.py lines 316 and 318: 'raise Exception(_(\"JSON file does not contain a list.\"))' \u2014 replace with 'raise forms.ValidationError(_(\"JSON file does not contain a list.\"))'. In app/eventyay/orga/forms/submission.py line 214: 'raise Exception(\"Cannot anonymise unsaved submission.\")' \u2014 replace with 'raise ValueError(\"Cannot anonymise unsaved submission.\")' since this is a programming error not a form error. In app/eventyay/base/models/organizer.py lines 48 and 73: check_access_permissions raises bare Exception with translated strings \u2014 replace with a new PermissionDenied (django.core.exceptions.PermissionDenied) or custom OrganizerAccessDenied(PermissionDenied) class.",
          "effort": "small",
          "issue_refs": [
            "review::.::holistic::error_consistency::err_security_bare_exception",
            "review::.::holistic::error_consistency::err_user_validation_bare_exception",
            "review::.::holistic::error_consistency::err-002"
          ]
        },
        {
          "title": "Fix FileCleanupMixin silent swallow and GeoCodeView mixed error response",
          "detail": "In app/eventyay/base/models/mixins.py line 184: FileCleanupMixin._delete_files() uses 'with suppress(Exception)' around value.delete(save=False). Replace with explicit 'try: value.delete(save=False) except OSError as e: logger.warning(\"Failed to delete file %s: %s\", value.name, e)'. Import logging at top of mixins.py if not already present (it is not). In app/eventyay/control/views/geo.py line 29: returns {'success': False, 'results': []} when neither opencagedata_apikey nor mapquest_apikey is set; line 32 returns the same structure for IOError. Differentiate: change line 29 return to JsonResponse({'success': False, 'error': 'no_api_key', 'results': []}) and line 32 return to JsonResponse({'success': False, 'error': 'network_error', 'results': []}). In app/eventyay/base/services/announcement.py: the @database_sync_to_async functions at lines 8, 15, 20, 32 do not handle DoesNotExist \u2014 wrap each in try/except Model.DoesNotExist and return None or re-raise as a named exception the consumer handles.",
          "effort": "small",
          "issue_refs": [
            "review::.::holistic::error_consistency::err_file_cleanup_silent_swallow",
            "review::.::holistic::error_consistency::err_geo_silent_mixed_failure",
            "review::.::holistic::error_consistency::err-001",
            "review::.::holistic::error_consistency::err-004"
          ]
        },
        {
          "title": "Audit and replace 30+ bare Exception() calls in production domain code",
          "detail": "In app/eventyay/base/models/mixins.py line 98: LogMixin.log_action calls LogEntry.objects.create() with no exception handling. If the DB write fails (connection lost, constraint violation), the exception propagates silently upward through business logic. Wrap lines 98-115 in 'try: ... except Exception: logger.exception(\"Failed to persist log entry for action %s\", action); return None'. Similarly in app/eventyay/base/models/base.py line 93-118 (LoggingMixin version), wrap the logentry.save() at line 113 in try/except. Additional bare Exception raises in base/models: confirm with grep -rn 'raise Exception(' app/eventyay/base/models/ -- targets include app/eventyay/base/models/mail.py line 406, app/eventyay/base/models/invoices.py line 246. Create app/eventyay/base/exceptions.py with domain exceptions: InvoiceDeleteError, MailTemplateError, ScheduleConflictError. Replace each raise Exception(...) with the typed variant.",
          "effort": "medium",
          "issue_refs": [
            "review::.::holistic::error_consistency::err-005",
            "review::.::holistic::error_consistency::err_bare_exception_domain_violations"
          ]
        }
      ],
      "depends_on_clusters": [
        "model-naming-and-base-cleanup"
      ]
    },
