    "settings-import-coupling": {
      "name": "settings-import-coupling",
      "description": "Fix module-scope settings snapshots and import-time coupling: TALK_HOSTNAME snapshot at base/models/event.py line 84, LANGUAGE_CODES_MAPPING computed at import time in common/language.py, base/__init__.py importing celery_app at module scope, app_cache populated without thread lock at base/signals.py",
      "issue_ids": [
        "review::.::holistic::initialization_coupling::IC-01",
        "review::.::holistic::initialization_coupling::IC-02",
        "review::.::holistic::initialization_coupling::IC-03",
        "review::.::holistic::initialization_coupling::IC-04"
      ],
      "created_at": "2026-03-15T09:39:17+00:00",
      "updated_at": "2026-03-16T07:07:27+00:00",
      "auto": false,
      "cluster_key": "",
      "action": null,
      "user_modified": true,
      "action_steps": [
        {
          "title": "Defer TALK_HOSTNAME and LANGUAGE_CODES_MAPPING from module scope to lazy properties",
          "detail": "In app/eventyay/base/models/event.py line 84: 'TALK_HOSTNAME = settings.TALK_HOSTNAME' is a module-scope snapshot. Replace with a function: 'def get_talk_hostname(): return settings.TALK_HOSTNAME' and update all 3+ call sites in event.py that reference TALK_HOSTNAME to call get_talk_hostname() instead. In app/eventyay/common/language.py line 9: 'LANGUAGE_CODES_MAPPING = {language.lower(): language for language in settings.LANGUAGES_INFORMATION}' \u2014 wrap in a functools.lru_cache function. In app/eventyay/eventyay_common/views/account/basic.py line 41: replace 'VALID_LANGUAGE_CODES = {code for code, __ in settings.LANGUAGES}' with a function.",
          "effort": "medium",
          "issue_refs": [
            "review::.::holistic::initialization_coupling::IC-01",
            "review::.::holistic::initialization_coupling::IC-02"
          ]
        },
        {
          "title": "Remove celery_app module-scope import from base/__init__.py and add lock to app_cache",
          "detail": "In app/eventyay/base/apps.py lines 8-30: the ready() method has 'from eventyay.celery_app import app as celery_app  # NOQA' inside try/except \u2014 this is acceptable but the import at line 30 'import eventyay.celery_app as celery  # NOQA' is a second trigger. Review if both are needed; keep only one and wrap in try/except ImportError. In app/eventyay/base/signals.py line 14: 'app_cache = {}' is a mutable global populated by _populate_app_cache() (line 17) without a threading.Lock(). Add 'import threading; _app_cache_lock = threading.Lock()' and wrap the _populate_app_cache() body with 'with _app_cache_lock:' to prevent race.",
          "effort": "small",
          "issue_refs": [
            "review::.::holistic::initialization_coupling::IC-03",
            "review::.::holistic::initialization_coupling::IC-04"
          ]
        },
        {
          "title": "Add tests for override_settings compatibility after deferring module-scope snapshots",
          "detail": "Write Django test using @override_settings in app/tests/stable/test_common.py: override TALK_HOSTNAME to a test value and call get_talk_hostname() (after refactor) to verify it returns the overridden value not the original. Do the same for LANGUAGE_CODES_MAPPING if it becomes a cached function \u2014 use functools.lru_cache clear between tests. Confirm these tests pass, demonstrating that override_settings now works correctly with the deferred getters.",
          "effort": "small",
          "issue_refs": [
            "review::.::holistic::initialization_coupling::IC-01",
            "review::.::holistic::initialization_coupling::IC-02"
          ]
        },
        {
          "title": "Audit for other module-scope settings snapshots across the codebase",
          "detail": "Run: grep -rn 'settings\\.' app/eventyay/ --include='*.py' | grep -v 'def \\|class \\|#\\|import' | grep -E '^[a-zA-Z_]+ = settings\\.' to find module-scope settings captures. Expected hits include TALK_HOSTNAME in app/eventyay/base/models/event.py, LANGUAGE_CODES_MAPPING in app/eventyay/common/language.py, and potentially more in config/ or helpers/. Compile a list and for each: measure whether stale values cause test failures under override_settings, then prioritize by risk.",
          "effort": "small",
          "issue_refs": [
            "review::.::holistic::initialization_coupling::IC-01",
            "review::.::holistic::initialization_coupling::IC-02"
          ]
        }
      ],
      "depends_on_clusters": [
        "ai-debt-cleanup"
      ]
    },
    "order-model-logic-fixes": {
      "name": "order-model-logic-fixes",
      "description": "Fix logic defects in base/models/orders.py and base/services/orders.py: _check_positions err accumulation inconsistency, user_cancel_allowed EXPIRED status exclusion without explanation, extend_order single-use closure with two call sites, get_schedule_exporter_content duplicated -my prefix check",
      "issue_ids": [
        "review::.::holistic::logic_clarity::lc-02",
        "review::.::holistic::logic_clarity::lc-06",
        "review::.::holistic::logic_clarity::lc-05",
        "review::.::holistic::low_level_elegance::lle-02",
        "review::.::holistic::low_level_elegance::lle-03",
        "review::.::holistic::low_level_elegance::lle-06"
      ],
      "created_at": "2026-03-15T09:39:43+00:00",
      "updated_at": "2026-03-15T10:29:34+00:00",
      "auto": false,
      "cluster_key": "",
      "action": null,
      "user_modified": true,
      "action_steps": [
        {
          "title": "Normalize _check_positions err accumulation pattern and add EXPIRED comment to user_cancel_allowed",
          "detail": "In app/eventyay/base/services/orders.py _check_positions (line 604): error accumulation mixes 'err = err or error_messages[...]' (keeps first error, lines 637/655/667/674/689/694/704/712/736/817/825/834/844/850/863/879) with 'err = error_messages[...]' (overwrites with last error, lines 644/725). Decide on one strategy (keep first error is more common): change lines 644 and 725 to use 'err = err or error_messages[...]' pattern to match the rest. In app/eventyay/base/models/orders.py line 613: user_cancel_allowed returns False for STATUS_EXPIRED \u2014 add inline comment explaining why EXPIRED is excluded even though cancel_allowed() treats it as cancelable (e.g., 'EXPIRED orders cannot be user-canceled because...').",
          "effort": "small",
          "issue_refs": [
            "review::.::holistic::logic_clarity::lc-02",
            "review::.::holistic::logic_clarity::lc-06"
          ]
        },
        {
          "title": "Inline extend_order closure, deduplicate get_schedule_exporter_content paths, extract magic sort constants",
          "detail": "In app/eventyay/base/services/orders.py lines 219-248: extend_order's inner change() closure is called twice (line 242 with was_expired=False, line 246 with was_expired=True). Inline it: replace the two change() calls with the function body directly, using if/else for the was_expired branching. In app/eventyay/agenda/views/utils.py lines 207-224: get_schedule_exporter_content checks '-my' in exporter.identifier three times (lines 207, 212, 224). Extract to a local variable 'is_my = \"-my\" in exporter.identifier' at the top and replace all three checks with 'is_my'.",
          "effort": "small",
          "issue_refs": [
            "review::.::holistic::logic_clarity::lc-05",
            "review::.::holistic::low_level_elegance::lle-02"
          ]
        },
        {
          "title": "Narrow bare except in update_user_profile_from_social",
          "detail": "In app/eventyay/features/social/utils.py line 38: bare 'except:' catches all exceptions including SystemExit and KeyboardInterrupt. Replace with 'except (requests.RequestException, OSError, ValueError) as e:' \u2014 the code downloads an avatar image (StoredFile.objects.create and sf.file.save), so network errors (RequestException), OS file errors (OSError), and content-type parsing errors (ValueError) are the expected failure modes. Keep the 'logging.exception(...)' call.",
          "effort": "trivial",
          "issue_refs": [
            "review::.::holistic::low_level_elegance::lle-03"
          ]
        }
      ],
      "depends_on_clusters": [
        "design-coherence-fixes"
      ]
    },
    "service-layer-cleanup": {
      "name": "service-layer-cleanup",
      "description": "Fix medium-severity service layer issues: replace apps.ready() opaque side-effect imports with explicit signal registration, replace update_announcement _meta.get_fields() reflection with static field list, merge CompatibleCountryField/CountryField duplicate to_internal_value logic, add raise/return to get_user_by_id/token/client_id None-on-DoesNotExist trio",
      "issue_ids": [
        "review::.::holistic::mid_level_elegance::mle-01",
        "review::.::holistic::mid_level_elegance::mle-02",
        "review::.::holistic::mid_level_elegance::mle-03",
        "review::.::holistic::mid_level_elegance::mle-04",
        "review::.::holistic::api_surface_coherence::AC-05",
        "review::.::holistic::logic_clarity::LC-02"
      ],
      "created_at": "2026-03-15T09:40:22+00:00",
      "updated_at": "2026-03-16T07:14:55+00:00",
      "auto": false,
      "cluster_key": "",
      "action": null,
      "user_modified": true,
      "action_steps": [
        {
          "title": "Replace apps.ready() implicit imports with explicit signal.connect() registration",
          "detail": "In app/eventyay/base/apps.py ready() (lines 8-25): side-effect imports like 'from . import exporter' at line 9 trigger signal registration implicitly. To make this explicit, find the signal.connect() calls in eventyay/base/exporter.py, eventyay/base/payment.py, etc. and move them into EventyayBaseConfig.ready() as direct calls: 'from eventyay.base.exporter import register_signals; register_signals()'. Repeat for all apps.py files in app/eventyay/ that use opaque side-effect imports in ready().",
          "effort": "medium",
          "issue_refs": [
            "review::.::holistic::mid_level_elegance::mle-01"
          ]
        },
        {
          "title": "Replace update_announcement _meta reflection and merge CompatibleCountryField duplicate logic",
          "detail": "In app/eventyay/base/services/announcement.py lines 33-48: update_announcement uses Announcement._meta.get_fields() for permitted_fields. The Announcement model (app/eventyay/base/models/announcement.py) has fields: id, event (FK), text (TextField), state (CharField). Replace _meta.get_fields() with explicit: 'PERMITTED_FIELDS = frozenset({\"text\", \"state\"})' at module level and use it instead. In app/eventyay/api/serializers/order.py lines 61-82: CompatibleCountryField.to_internal_value and CountryField.to_internal_value are identical (line 62 = line 73). Extract to a shared _country_internal_value(data, field_name) free function and call it from both.",
          "effort": "small",
          "issue_refs": [
            "review::.::holistic::mid_level_elegance::mle-02",
            "review::.::holistic::mid_level_elegance::mle-03"
          ]
        },
        {
          "title": "Convert get_user_by_id/token/client_id trio to raise exceptions or Optional annotations",
          "detail": "In app/eventyay/base/services/user.py lines 26-42: get_user_by_id, get_user_by_token_id, get_user_by_client_id all return None on DoesNotExist with no annotation. Add '-> Optional[User]' return type annotation to all three. Alternatively, if callers should always expect a User, raise User.DoesNotExist instead of returning None. Check all callers (search 'get_user_by_id(' app/eventyay/) to determine which pattern is safer. At minimum, add the Optional[User] annotation so callers can see the None contract.",
          "effort": "trivial",
          "issue_refs": [
            "review::.::holistic::mid_level_elegance::mle-04"
          ]
        },
        {
          "title": "Write tests confirming explicit signal registration behavior in apps.ready()",
          "detail": "After converting app/eventyay/base/apps.py ready() to use explicit signal.connect() calls: write a test in app/tests/stable/test_common.py that imports an Order and triggers the order_placed signal manually (Order.order_placed.send(sender=Order, ...)), then asserts that the connected handler ran. This test will catch regressions where signal wiring is accidentally broken by a future refactor. Use Django's signal receiver override mechanism to isolate the test.",
          "effort": "small",
          "issue_refs": [
            "review::.::holistic::mid_level_elegance::mle-01"
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
